---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
const email = 'hello@lifeatthefrontier.com';
---
<LegalPage
  heading="Privacy"
  path="/privacy"
  updated="25 November 2026"
  description="How Life at the Frontier handles your personal information. No cookies, no tracking, and your email address is used only to send the newsletter."
>
  <p class="lf-doc-lead">
    Life at the Frontier is a podcast created and hosted by Mehdi Nayebi. This page explains what
    personal information we collect through lifeatthefrontier.com, why, and what you can do about it.
    The short version: we collect as little as we can, we never sell it, and this website uses no
    cookies and no tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible for your information</h2>
  <p>
    Mehdi Nayebi, as the creator of Life at the Frontier, is responsible for the personal information
    described here. You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with any question or
    request about your information.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your email address, if you subscribe to the newsletter.</strong> We use it only to send
      you The Frontier Brief and messages about your subscription. We ask you to confirm your address
      before we send anything. Our legal basis is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you send us, if you email us.</strong> We use it to reply to you and to deal with
      your request. Our legal basis is our legitimate interest in answering the people who contact us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Basic technical data when you visit.</strong> Like every website, our hosting provider
      receives your IP address, browser type and the pages requested, so that it can deliver the site
      and protect it from abuse. We do not use this data to identify or profile you. Our legal basis is
      our legitimate interest in running a secure website.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not collect any other information through this website. We do not ask for your name, and we
    do not collect sensitive information.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies. It uses no analytics, no advertising tags, no social media pixels and
    no third-party fonts or scripts. That is why you do not see a cookie banner. If we ever add privacy
    friendly analytics, we will update this page first.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We never sell, rent or trade your personal information, and we do not share it for advertising. We
    share it only with the service providers that help us run the site and the newsletter, and only
    as far as they need it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong>, which hosts this website.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our email newsletter provider</strong>, which stores subscriber addresses and sends the
      newsletter on our behalf.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Our email provider</strong>, which handles messages sent to our contact address.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may only use your information to provide their service to us. We may also disclose
    information if the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our providers process data in the United States and other countries. Where information
    about people in the UK or European Economic Area is transferred, we rely on the safeguards the law
    recognises, such as standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Newsletter: until you unsubscribe, after which your address is removed from our mailing list.</li>
    <li>Emails: for as long as we need them to deal with your message, and then deleted.</li>
    <li>Technical data: kept by our hosting provider for a short period under its own policy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you have the right to ask for a copy of your information, to have it
    corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict how we use it, to receive it in a portable format, and
    to withdraw your consent at any time. You can unsubscribe from the newsletter with the link in every
    email. To make any other request, write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We will
    reply within one month.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are in California: we do not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined
    in California law, and we will not treat you differently for using your privacy rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not happy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to your local data
    protection authority. We would appreciate the chance to put it right first.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website and the newsletter are not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly
    collect their information. If you believe a child has given us their details, please tell us and we
    will delete them.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served only over an encrypted connection, and we limit who can access subscriber data.
    No system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how we handle your information, we will update this page and the date at the top. If a
    change is significant, we will tell newsletter subscribers by email before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
